cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the archived software release and the associated manuscript."

title: "Reproducibility Software for Numerical Certification and Approximation Benchmarking of an Experimentally Anchored Soft-Core Atom-Ion Radial Hamiltonian"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Abu Ayyash"
    given-names: "Mohammad Y."
    affiliation: "Al-Quds University"

  - family-names: "Barghouthi"
    given-names: "Imad A."
    affiliation: "Al-Quds University"

version: "1.0.5"
date-released: 2026-08-28

license: MIT

abstract: >-
  Reproducibility source code, tests, execution metadata, and selected
  generated outputs supporting numerical certification and fixed-operator
  approximation benchmarking of an experimentally anchored effective
  soft-core atom-ion radial Hamiltonian. The software includes fourth-order
  finite-difference calculations, continuum extrapolation, independent
  Numerov validation, WKB quantization, variational calculations,
  perturbative-breakdown diagnostics, non-perturbative
  harmonic-oscillator-basis diagonalization, regulator-dependence analysis,
  angular-sector diagnostics, zero-energy boundary calculations, and
  continuum-certified trap-frequency sensitivity over 1.10-1.30 MHz using
  fixed-r_c and continuum-recalibrated-r_c protocols. The numerical precision
  reported by the software characterizes the selected frozen operator and
  must not be interpreted as comparable physical accuracy for the complete
  Paul-trap system or its dynamical formation process.

keywords:
  - atom-ion
  - effective Hamiltonian
  - soft-core potential
  - radial Hamiltonian
  - numerical certification
  - finite-difference method
  - continuum extrapolation
  - Numerov method
  - WKB quantization
  - variational method
  - perturbation theory
  - harmonic-oscillator basis
  - regulator dependence
  - trap-frequency sensitivity
  - reproducible research

